de the running band; -1 = never saturated. Main curve starts at 50 (paper, diversity.tex line 13); stopping_point_start100 uses init 100 as the notebook did.","ordering_caveat":"The saved embeddings are NOT in generation order: EvaluatorModelWrapper.get_motion_embeddings sorts by motion length (descending) and returns that order, so \"the first n descriptions\" in the notebook are the n LONGEST motions. generation_order (only for realworld/pamap2/usc-had) re-embeds the clips in prompt-index order with the same evaluator (verified to reproduce the saved vectors, median NN distance < 0.004 vs norm ~10.6).","paper_claim":"IMUGPT 2.0 diversity.tex line 47: most saturation points fall within ~400-600 descriptions. That claim is about the text-description saturation algorithm (text embeddings, not in the repo); this file is motion-embedding diversity.","stochasticity":"Stopping points depend on the random resampling: re-running the notebook on realworld_2000 with 3 seeds moved e.g. standing from 488 to 1161 and running from 620 to 651. Treat single values as indicative.","notebook_check":"Re-running this code on realworld_2000 with init 100 reproduced the notebook saved outputs closely: climb down 239/262 (nb 239), climb up 199-228 (nb 199), jumping 228-250 (nb 250), lying 228 (nb 239), sitting 228-239 (nb 228), standing 488 (nb 488), walking 262-288 (nb 262); running 620-651 vs nb 443 (nb used calc_steps(2000) on 2,024 rows)."},"stopping_point_summary":{"notebook_order_start50":{"median":72.5,"min":60,"max":427,"n_activities":12,"n_never_saturated":0,"frac_in_400_600":0.08},"notebook_order_start100":{"median":385.0,"min":158,"max":591,"n_activities":12,"n_never_saturated":0,"frac_in_400_600":0.5},"generation_order_start50":{"median":155.5,"min":60,"max":626,"n_activities":12,"n_never_saturated":0,"frac_in_400_600":0.08},"generation_order_start100":{"median":422.5,"min":126,"max":717,"n_activities":12,"n_never_saturated":0,"frac_in_400_600":0.5}},"saturation_points_used_in_paper":{"per_activity":{"climbing down stairs":488,"climbing up stairs":422,"jumping":465,"lying":422,"riding down elevator":488,"riding up elevator":465,"running":443,"sitting":465,"standing":422,"walking clockwise":537,"walking counter-clockwise":563,"walking forward":422},"median":465.0,"mean":466.8,"min":422,"max":563,"frac_in_400_600":1.0,"source":"size of motion_embedding/t2m-gpt/usc-had_1000_optimal/<act>.npy = number of descriptions kept by the saturation-point algorithm (init 100, +5%/step; which modality drove it, text or motion, is not recorded in the repo - the paper says text); these sets presumably underlie the With Saturation Point rows of tables/algo_eval.tex. Values are all on the calc_steps(.,0.05,100) grid."}}